  "answer": "Based on current web results retrieved on October 27, 2026, the typical hydration percentage recommended for a beginner sourdough loaf is between 65% and 70% [W5, W6, W7]. Some sources note that the easiest range for beginners to handle can start anywhere from 60% up to 68%–70% [W6, W7], while hydration levels under 70% are generally aimed at novice bakers [W1]. \n\n* **Handling and Structure:** Dough within the 65% to 70% range is balanced, manageable, forgiving, and holds good structural integrity [W6, W7]. It provides beginner-friendly handling and consistent results, allowing new bakers to focus on mastering fermentation timing and shaping fundamentals rather than struggling with overly wet, sticky dough [W5, W6].\n* **Crumb and Progression:** While loaf recipes below 70% hydration may produce a tighter or moderate crumb [W1, W5], experts advise beginners to bake their first 5 to 10 loaves between 65% and 70% before progressively increasing hydration to the standard artisan range of 70% to 75% or higher [W5, W6, W7]."
